planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
- On a real fs.WriteStream, destroy() before the open completes waits for the open, then closes the fd, then emits 'close', so .closed stays false until then. A PassThrough or plain Writable mock closes synchronously, which is why the existing LogRotator.test.ts cases keep rejecting at once.
- Writable's `destroy` constructor option replaces _destroy; never calling its callback gives a stream that never closes.
- vitest's default fake timers do not fake process.nextTick, so stream 'close' still fires under vi.useFakeTimers (the existing timeout case shows it).
